# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vivado generated output.
#
# Everything here is rebuilt from LisaFPGA.xpr plus the sources, constraints and IP definitions,
# and it comes to roughly 145MB, so none of it belongs in git.
#
# NOTE: LisaFPGA.runs itself is deliberately NOT ignored. This repo already tracks the IP-level
# synthesis checkpoints (clock_divider.dcp, dotck_mmcm.dcp, hdmi_clock_divider.dcp) and the run
# scripts under it, and a blanket ignore would be confusing next to those. The entries below are
# narrow on purpose: they cover only files and directories that were never tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

LisaFPGA.cache/
LisaFPGA.gen/
LisaFPGA.hw/
LisaFPGA.ip_user_files/
LisaFPGA.srcs/utils_1/

# Per-run scratch, logs and journals
.Xil/
LisaFPGA.runs/.jobs/
*.jou
*.log
*.str
*.backup.jou
*.backup.log

# Whole run directories that have never been tracked. The IP runs here are regenerated by
# add_1024x768_clocks.tcl / add_settings_ila.tcl, and synth_1/impl_1 outputs by a build.
LisaFPGA.runs/synth_1/
LisaFPGA.runs/settings_ila_synth_1/
LisaFPGA.runs/hdmi_clock_divider_1024x768_synth_1/

# Implementation outputs. Kept narrow rather than a blanket *.dcp, because the three IP-level
# .dcp files under LisaFPGA.runs/*_synth_1/ ARE tracked.
LisaFPGA.runs/impl_1/top*.dcp
LisaFPGA.runs/impl_1/*.rpt
LisaFPGA.runs/impl_1/*.rpx
LisaFPGA.runs/impl_1/*.vdi
# Timing-analysis byproduct. Named specifically rather than impl_1/*.txt, because clockInfo.txt
# and htr.txt in the same directory ARE tracked.
LisaFPGA.runs/impl_1/tight_setup_hold_pins.txt

# ILA capture exports from the settings-flash debugging (findings are written up in CLAUDE.md)
ila_*.csv

# RISC-V toolchain for the USB soft-CPU firmware (xPack riscv-none-elf-gcc, ~2GB unpacked). See
# docs/usb_softcpu_host_design.md for the version and download source.
/tools/toolchain/
